{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "TriageWiseProdrome — red-flag layer cases (reqs 1.31, 1.33)",
    "validates": "RedFlagLayer.check(intake, score) — AND/OR tree evaluation, flag_tier, and the invariant that flags NEVER change the score",
    "how_to_use": "Each case: build the intake + a SeverityResult (score_in), call check(), assert the fired flag_ids, flag_tier, and that score_out == score_in. Positive AND negative cases per flag prove the AND-logic actually gates.",
    "invariants": [
      "Flags never change severity_score or esi_level — score_out must equal score_in in every case.",
      "flag_tier written to patient_severity = min tier among fired flags (1 beats 2 beats 3); no flag => tier 3.",
      "A flag fires only when ALL its AND-conditions hold; an OR-group needs only one branch.",
      "Symptoms / conditions are matched by stable key (fast_positive, heavy_bleeding, ...), never display text."
    ],
    "helpers_assumed": {
      "all_vitals_normal": "no vital scoring rule fired EXCEPT the pain rule (rule 7) — pain is excluded on purpose so flag 3 ('all vitals normal AND pain>=7') can fire. Derived by inspecting the SeverityResult's fired drivers, ignoring the pain driver. NB: despite the name, high pain alone does NOT make this false.",
      "count_borderline_vitals": "count of HR/RR/SBP/temp in BORDERLINE bands (SpO2 excluded)",
      "BORDERLINE": "HR 90-99, RR 21-24, SBP 90-99, temp 99.5-100.3F",
      "SHOCK": "HR>=100 AND SBP<=100"
    },
    "score_in_note": "score_in is the SeverityResult the engine already produced; only the fields the red-flag layer reads (esi_level, severity_score, drivers→all_vitals_normal) matter. Vitals for all_vitals_normal are carried on the intake."
  },
